WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.474
The kit turns every provider's notice
into one record with one of six kinds:

2
00:00:05.474 --> 00:00:10.275
maintenance, retirement, advisory,
security, change and incident.

3
00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:13.400
The table maps each provider's
own types onto them.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.313
Two rows are worth a closer look.

5
00:00:15.313 --> 00:00:20.081
A retirement in Azure is a health advisory
with the subtype retirement, and in

6
00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:25.074
AWS the kit infers it from a scheduled
change whose event code names a retirement.

7
00:00:25.074 --> 00:00:28.412
That second one is the
kit's rule, not AWS's.

8
00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:31.313
And Google Cloud's column is almost empty:

9
00:00:31.313 --> 00:00:36.176
its Personalized Service Health API
has a single category, incident.

10
00:00:36.176 --> 00:00:41.162
Each record also says whether action
is required, by when, and who said so.

11
00:00:41.162 --> 00:00:46.588
Microsoft 365, Oracle and AWS
each have a field for that.

12
00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:51.218
Azure doesn't, so the kit applies
its own stated rule: a retirement is

13
00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:55.920
due at the advisory's end, which
Microsoft Learn says is its end time.
